          465.0,
          916.0
        ],
        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "A 100-ml, two-necked, round-bottomed flask equipped with a magnetic stirrer, nitrogen gas inlet tube, and calcium chloride drying tube was charged with 26 mmol of the 1-aminoanthraquinone and 75 ml of dry NMP. The mixture was stirred at $0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$for 0.5 hr. Then 21.6 ml of propylene oxide was added, and after about 3 min, 30 mmol of $^ { 3 , 5 \\cdot }$-dinitrobenzoyl chloride was added and the mixture was stirred at $0 ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }$for 0.5 hr. The temperature was raised to room temperature and the solution was stirred for 6 hr. The product was precipitated by pouring the content of the flask into water. Then it was filtered, washed with hot water, and dried overnight under vacuum at 708C. The yield of the reaction was about 92%."
      },
      "confidence": {
        "score": 0.9
      }
    },
    {
      "step_id": "ps002",
      "process_type": "other",
      "input_sample_ids": [],
      "output_sample_ids": [
        "s011"
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "yield": "95%"
      },
      "evidence": {
        "block_id": "P_1_28",
        "page": 1,
        "bbox": [
          495.0,
          516.0,
          907.0,
          574.0
        ],
        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "The aforementioned procedure was applied to the synthesis of the dinitro compound. However, 2-aminoanthraquinone was used instead of 1-aminoanthraquinone. The yield of the reaction was about 95%."
      },
      "confidence": {
        "score": 0.9
      }
    },
    {
      "step_id": "ps003",
      "process_type": "other",
      "input_sample_ids": [
        "s010"
